    "['isis circuit-type [parameter1]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1 disable', 'parent_command': ['set interfaces [parameter1]'], 'root': 'set interfaces [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': \"Here's the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `isis circuit-type level-1` command:\\n\\n##\\nset protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1 disable\\n##\\n\\nNote: \\n1. In Juniper, you would specify the actual interface name (like ge-1/0/0.0) instead of `<interface-name>`\\n2. Juniper uses a slightly different approach - by default IS-IS runs at both levels, so we disable level 2 to make it level-1 only (which is equivalent to Cisco's `level-1` setting)\\n3. The command would need to be repeated for each interface where you want this configuration\", 'trans_template': 'set protocols isis interface <interface-name> level 1 disable'}]]": 1,
